ear facility  and now in the last hour the iranians  describing this as an attack  if they're saying this is an attack  first of all how much damage do you  think could have been sustained here  well it's not clear what  what happened exactly at the facility  obviously uh there are conflicting  reports but  his latest uh remarks suggest that there  were there has been an attack  we don't know what kind of attack is it  a cyber or  an act of uh you know uh physical  sabotage  we don't know that we we are yet to hear  about that but obviously uh the  conclusion is that  uh the the there is an act of  sabotage and uh and uh uh obviously  the israelis are to blame in such uh  circumstances  because uh previous you know uh  incidents  uh have uh pointed to israel as well so  it has a track record of the week  well there is no proof right now as to  israel's responsibility but certainly as  you say iran in the past has  blamed israel for such attacks there was  a fire at the natanz  facility last year which tehran blamed  on israel  this is all coming as uh the nuclear  talks are about to resume with the  united states  trying to revive the 2015 nuclear deal  if it is an attack and an act of  sabotage as the iranians are saying  how might it affect their position in  the negotiations  this can potentially have a negative  effect on the  negotiations obviously the israelis have  an interest  uh and and they have you know announced  uh  time and time again that they  would not like to see the jcpoa being  revived  and the united states getting back to  its commitments in  the jcpoa so the iranians will be asking  themselves whether these  kinds of attacks are in coordination  with the united states or not because  uh previously during the negotiations  leading up to the 2015 nuclear deal with  iran  the the united states has proved that it  can put a cap on the israeli  activities assassinations within iran  ukrainian  nuclear facilities or against its uh  scientists right  but now obviously the israelis are  increasing their attacks but there is no  uh acts uh on the part of the united  states  you you keep talking about israel and  the iranians uh certainly keep talking  about israel as  uh being responsible of what they're  calling act of sabotage but  israel is not the only country that has  concerns about the resumption  of the 2015 nuclear deal the saudis are  also very wary  it's not only about the intention it's  about the capabilities  the israelis uh many believe in iran  many believe that  the israelis and the united states are  the only parties that  are capable of doing these kinds of  attacks within iran  the saudis have didn't show previously  any  uh such capabilities so the points are  there the blame is pointed to the  israelis or the united states  and in in another scenario but obviously  uh taking the current negotiations  indirect negotiations between iran and  the united states into account  it's uh you know it's easy to conclude  that the  israelis who are on their toes uh on the  revival of the jcpoa are willing to do  uh something to affect that negatively  thank you for that thank you very much  for bringing us the viewpoint from iran  there  hassan hamadian joining us from tehran  thank you for your time  in other news jordan's king abdullah and  his half-brother have appeared together  for the first time since their political  rift  former crown prince hamza joined the

